---
// pages/privacy.astro — Privacy Policy
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { buildTitle, buildCanonical } from '../lib/seo';
import { business, phone } from '../data/client.config';

const title = buildTitle("Privacy Policy");
const canonicalUrl = buildCanonical("/privacy");
---

<BaseLayout title={title} canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}>
  <section class="py-16 sm:py-20 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 prose prose-green prose-lg">

      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm not-prose">Last updated: April 21, 2026</p>

      <p>
        Environmental Forest Products ("EFP," "we," "us," or "our") operates the website at
        <a href={business.domain}>{business.domain}</a>. This Privacy Policy explains what
        information we collect, how we use it, and your choices regarding that information.
        By using this website or submitting a form, you agree to the practices described below.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

      <h3>Information You Provide Directly</h3>
      <p>When you submit a contact or estimate form, we collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>First and last name</li>
        <li>Phone number</li>
        <li>Email address (optional)</li>
        <li>County and location details</li>
        <li>Project description and property information you choose to share</li>
        <li>SMS consent selections (marketing and/or transactional, as described below)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Automatically Collected Information</h3>
      <p>
        When you visit our website, we automatically collect standard server and browser data,
        including your IP address, browser type and version, pages visited, time spent on pages,
        and referring URL. This data is collected through Google Analytics 4 on an anonymous,
        aggregated basis and is used solely to understand site performance.
      </p>

      <h3>Spam Protection</h3>
      <p>
        Our forms use Cloudflare Turnstile, a CAPTCHA-alternative service, to prevent automated
        spam submissions. Cloudflare may collect technical data (such as IP address and browser
        fingerprint) to evaluate whether a form submission is human-generated. This data is
        processed by Cloudflare under their own
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <p>Information you provide is used exclusively to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Respond to your inquiry and schedule site assessments or consultations</li>
        <li>Send follow-up communications directly related to your request</li>
        <li>Send SMS messages where you have explicitly opted in (see Section 3 below)</li>
        <li>Improve our website content and user experience using anonymous analytics data</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not sell, rent, lease, or share your personal information with third parties
        for their marketing purposes. We do not use your contact information for any purpose
        unrelated to your inquiry with EFP.
      </p>

      <h2>3. SMS Communications</h2>
      <p>
        Our contact forms offer two separate, voluntary SMS consent options:
      </p>

      <h3>Marketing SMS</h3>
      <p>
        If you check the marketing SMS consent box, you agree to receive promotional text
        messages from Environmental Forest Products, which may include information about
        seasonal services, forestry tips, and special offers. Message frequency may vary.
        Message and data rates may apply.
      </p>

      <h3>Non-Marketing (Transactional) SMS</h3>
      <p>
        If you check the transactional SMS consent box, you agree to receive non-promotional
        text messages from Environmental Forest Products related to your inquiry, including
        appointment confirmations, scheduling coordination, and responses to your specific
        requests. Message and data rates may apply.
      </p>

      <h3>Opting Out</h3>
      <p>
        You may opt out of either type of SMS message at any time by replying <strong>STOP</strong>
        to any message you receive. Reply <strong>HELP</strong> for assistance. Opting in to
        either or both SMS types is entirely voluntary. Declining or withdrawing consent does
        not affect your ability to receive consultations or services from EFP.
      </p>

      <h3>SMS Provider</h3>
      <p>
        SMS communications are facilitated through CRST Web, our third-party CRM and messaging
        platform. Contact information and consent status you provide through our forms is
        transmitted to and stored in our CRM account. We do not share your information with
        any other third-party messaging providers.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Cookies and Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use Google Analytics 4 (GA4) to collect anonymous, aggregated data about how visitors
        use our website — pages visited, session duration, traffic sources, and device type.
        GA4 uses cookies to distinguish unique sessions. This data does not identify you personally.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can opt out of Google Analytics tracking by installing the
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on
        </a>. You can also manage cookie preferences through your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Online Calculators and Estimating Tools</h2>
      <p>
        Our website includes free estimating calculators (land clearing cost, timber value,
        tree removal cost, and 480-a tax savings). These tools perform all calculations
        locally in your browser. No data you enter into a calculator is transmitted to our
        servers or stored by us unless you separately submit a contact form.
      </p>
      <p>
        Calculator outputs are estimates only and do not constitute a formal appraisal, quote,
        or professional opinion. See our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> for full disclaimer.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
      <p>
        Contact information submitted through our forms is retained in our CRM (CRST Web)
        for as long as we maintain an active or prospective business relationship, or as required
        by applicable law. Anonymous Google Analytics data is retained per Google's standard
        data retention settings (14 months by default). You may request deletion of your personal
        data by contacting us directly.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Data Security</h2>
      <p>
        All data transmitted between your browser and this website is encrypted via HTTPS/TLS.
        Form submissions are transmitted to our CRM via secured webhook. We take reasonable
        technical and organizational precautions to protect your information. However, no method
        of electronic transmission is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        This website is not directed to children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly
        collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has submitted
        personal information to us, contact us at the address below and we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Third-Party Links</h2>
      <p>
        Our website contains links to external sites, including government agencies (NY DEC,
        Cornell Cooperative Extension) and industry resources. We are not responsible for the
        privacy practices or content of those sites. We encourage you to review their privacy
        policies independently.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Your Rights</h2>
      <p>
        You have the right to request access to, correction of, or deletion of personal
        information we hold about you. To exercise these rights, contact us using the
        information below. We will respond within a reasonable time period and in accordance
        with applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will update the
        "Last updated" date at the top of this page. Continued use of the website after changes
        are posted constitutes your acceptance of the updated policy. We encourage you to review
        this page periodically.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, how your data is handled, or to
        request deletion of your information, contact us at:
      </p>
      <address class="not-italic">
        Environmental Forest Products<br />
        Sullivan County, New York<br />
        <a href={`tel:${phone.trackingTel}`}>{business.phone}</a><br />
        <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>
      </address>

    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
